# Belt and braces for the Docker build context.
#
# backend/Dockerfile currently uses explicit COPY statements (pyproject.toml,
# alembic.ini, alembic/, app/), so .env cannot reach the image today. This file
# exists so that stays true if anyone ever simplifies those to `COPY . .` -- a
# one-line change that would otherwise bake a live RESEND_API_KEY into every layer
# of a published image, where deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it.
#
# The upload-side equivalent is .gcloudignore, which is the one that actually
# matters for `gcloud run deploy --source .`. Keep the two in sync.

.env
.env.*
*.pem
*-service-account*.json

.venv/
venv/

tests/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
htmlcov/
.coverage

.git/
.gitignore
